      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Thanks for the report! For the case of the Allow FBT toggle not hiding the button, the Pico motion trackers calibration is considered to be in a different category from our in-app FBT calibration. The Pico motion trackers button opens an OS level calibration app which operates separately from VRC. Some users will calibrate even before launching VRC, so we don't view it as being as closely tied to our FBT calibration as the Calibrate FBT button and therefore intentionally don't hide it.\n\nAs far as the button text being Pico or PICO, for a change to take place here we'd need to receive the request for change through official channels from Pico. However your report on this has been noted internally as well.\n\nWith both of those points not being currently mapped to an action item I'll close this Canny for now, though once again thank you for the report!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
